    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183-a1">

                <pb facs="0328" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg266"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 98.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Welsh to Lord
                            Salisbury</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-05-31"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 31,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Referring to your note of the 8th
                    ultimo, in reference to the monetary conference proposed by my government, I
                    have the honor to acquaint your lordship <pb facs="0329" n="267" xml:id="pg267"
                    /> that I received yesterday a telegraphic dispatch from the Assistant Secretary
                    of State, requesting me to telegraph the answer of Great Britain to the
                    proposal, and the date thereof. Will your lordship kindly inform me when it is
                    probable that I may have the pleasure of hearing from Her Majesty’s Government
                    in relation to this matter?</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN WELSH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
